    "text": "Chicago Bears TE Cole Kmet (knee) was carted off during the Week 7 game against the New England Patriots with a knee injury and did not return.\nSOURCE: Ian Rapoport\nChicago Bears TE Cole Kmet (knee) was carted off during the Week 7 game against the New England Patriots with a knee injury and did not return.\nSOURCE: Ian Rapoport\nWhy it Matters: It certainly looks like Kmet could be dealing with a serious knee injury, and if he misses extended time, it should mean a few more targets for the rest of Chicago's pass catchers. Colston Loveland, who has already started to return to form the last two games, could be the main beneficiary.\nThis article originally appeared on USA TODAY: Cole Kmet exits Week 7 game against New England\nReporting by Brian Polking, USA TODAY / USA TODAY\nUSA TODAY Network via Reuters Connect\nSorry, an error occurred.\nAlready Subscribed!\nCancel anytime\nThank you .\nYour account has been registered, and you are now logged in.\nCheck your email for details.\nSubmitting this form below will send a message to your email with a link to change your password.\nAn email message containing instructions on how to reset your password has been sent to the email address listed on your account.\nNo promotional rates found.\nSecure & Encrypted\nThank you.\nYour gift purchase was successful! Your purchase was successful, and you are now logged in.\n| Rate: | |\n| Begins: | |\n| Transaction ID: |\nA receipt was sent to your email.",
